cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Stepthrough in research, cite the Zenodo record for the version you used."
type: software
title: "Stepthrough: screen recordings to walkthrough steps and interface pathways"
version: "1.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Jin
    given-names: 'H. "Kevin"'
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24159850
repository-code: "https://github.com/j-nivekk/Stepthrough"
url: "https://github.com/j-nivekk/Stepthrough"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Stepthrough is a local-first research tool that turns screen recordings into
  chronological walkthrough screenshots and interface pathways. It combines
  stable-screen detection with manual review, titles, annotations and screen
  relationships. Researchers can export screenshots, CSV and JSON step data,
  structured pathways and SVG diagrams. Text recognition is optional.
keywords:
  - screen recordings
  - walkthrough method
  - interface research
  - interface pathways
  - research software
